MDL103, F1, F12: in a file with Windows (CRLF) line endings, an empty line is
"\r\n": the pre-processor counts the '\r' as content and turns it into
"\r= 1", so GLib rejects the file. mydumper ignores all of it, still connects
through [client] (the client library strips the '\r') and exits 0, with
users.email in plaintext.
-- scenario --
tool: mydumper
versions: >= v0.19.3-1
args: --defaults-file /work/defaults.cnf --database app
lint: MDL103, MDL405
expect config-loaded: false
expect exit: 0
expect connected: true
expect column app.users.email: plaintext
-- defaults.cnf.esc --
[client]\r\nhost=mysql\r\nuser=e2e\r\npassword=e2e-password\r\n\r\n[mydumper]\r\nthreads=2\r\n\r\n[`app`.`users`]\r\n`email`=random_string\r\n
